# Optional overrides — mspbots-agent-db has no required env vars.
# Authentication is per-request via three headers (provided by the MCP caller):
#   X-API-Key        Platform-issued EdDSA JWT. Forwarded verbatim as
#                    "Authorization: Bearer <token>" to the pg-data-ingest
#                    API — this is the only credential type pg-data-ingest's
#                    own upcoming release still accepts (pg-data-ingest's
#                    own, unrelated X-API-Key credential is being removed
#                    there; see README "Known Gaps"). Renamed from
#                    X-MSP-Token on 2026-09-23; the old name is still
#                    honoured as a fallback for pre-rename credentials.
#   X-MSP-Host       Base host for the Agent Data Core API, e.g.
#                    https://agentint.mspbots.ai — this server appends
#                    "/apps/pg-data-ingest/api/agent-data/agents/<agentId>/..."
#                    to it.
#   X-MSP-Tenant-Id  Not app-level auth — the shared APISIX gateway needs
#                    this to route to the right tenant's pod (pg-data-ingest
#                    is one pod per tenant). Forwarded as X_Tenant_ID.
#
# Separately, every pg-data-ingest data call also needs an app-level
# tenant_id query param (checked against the JWT's own tenant claim). This
# server resolves that itself via GET /whoami using X-API-Key — it is
# NOT the same value as X-MSP-Tenant-Id above and is never taken from a
# header or tool argument (see api_client.AgentDataClient docstring).
#
# agent_id is NOT a header — every agent-scoped tool takes it as a plain
# argument (see README "Known Gaps" for the isolation tradeoff this
# implies). mspbotsagentdb_list_agents is the one tool with no agent_id.

MCP_HTTP_PORT=8080
MCP_HTTP_HOST=0.0.0.0
